1
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:13,440
You're my one and only bro.

2
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:15,040
From now on, I'll only listen to you.

3
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:18,680
I had my reasons for doing this.

4
00:00:19,240 --> 00:00:20,200
Reasons?

5
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:21,080
What reasons?

6
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:25,960
I stole the crystals for my sister.

7
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:27,240
Your sister?

8
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:32,360
I did this just to make more money.

9
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:34,800
So my sister could live a better life.

10
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:35,920
My sister,

11
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:39,120
she grew up without a dad's love or a mom's care.

12
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:41,280
I worked my heart out.

13
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:42,600
Worked so hard to make money.

14
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:46,200
Just to give her a proper birthday celebration.

15
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:48,360
Am I wrong?

16
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:49,760
Your sister's birthday is coming?

17
00:00:51,960 --> 00:00:54,640
But that doesn't seem to be the main issue here.

18
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:55,840
Then,

19
00:00:56,960 --> 00:00:58,560
why don’t your parents care about her?

20
00:00:58,720 --> 00:00:59,840
Aren’t you two siblings?

21
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:01,840
Bro,

22
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:04,040
you don’t know the full story.

23
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:06,120
It’s a long story.

24
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:09,040
Actually, my sister and I are half-siblings.

25
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:10,639
Her mom and my dad,

26
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:12,680
got divorced when she was little.

27
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:13,800
And my dad,

28
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:14,840
later met my mom,

29
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:15,680
and had me.

30
00:01:16,080 --> 00:01:19,080
Meanwhile, her mom started a new family

31
00:01:19,240 --> 00:01:20,520
and had another child.

32
00:01:20,840 --> 00:01:21,560
So,

33
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:23,760
my sister was like a ball, being

34
00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:25,520
passed around.

35
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:26,800
Passed around.

36
00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:29,640
So,

37
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:32,320
my sister has always felt like an extra.

38
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:34,320
She’s had it that bad?

39
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:37,080
Only more,

40
00:01:38,040 --> 00:01:38,920
never less.

41
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:48,200
Take good care of my sister in the future, okay?

42
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:49,280
Future brother-in-law.

43
00:01:51,960 --> 00:01:52,600
Well, nothing else to say.

44
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:53,560
The misunderstanding has been cleared up.

45
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:54,800
I’ll head out now.

46
00:01:54,920 --> 00:01:55,560
Bye, bro-in-law.

47
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:13,360
You're awake.

48
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:16,480
What's going on?

49
00:02:17,320 --> 00:02:18,960
Such a fancy breakfast so early in the morning.

50
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:22,360
These...

51
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,080
are all prepared for you.

52
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:25,840
For me?

53
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:27,800
Qi Miao,

54
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:29,480
happy birthday!

55
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:34,440
If you hadn’t said anything, I would’ve forgotten it’s my birthday.

56
00:02:34,840 --> 00:02:35,600
Thanks!

57
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:37,720
Come on, our relationship...

58
00:02:38,280 --> 00:02:39,000
no need to say thank you.

59
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:40,400
Bro,

60
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:43,600
what’s going on between you and my sister now?

61
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:45,640
We’ve already reached...

62
00:02:50,160 --> 00:02:51,480
Uh, the weather’s a bit dry.

63
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:53,240
Just eat your breakfast.

64
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:54,320
Sis,

65
00:02:54,480 --> 00:02:56,040
we're all adults here.

66
00:02:56,520 --> 00:02:57,360
What’s there to be shy about?

67
00:02:57,800 --> 00:02:58,840
Shut your mouth.

68
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:00,480
Even eating can’t stop you from talking, huh?

69
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:02,880
Qi Miao,

70
00:03:04,240 --> 00:03:05,160
should we...

71
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:06,960
take this chance on your birthday to invite your parents over?

72
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:08,680
That way, I can also get to meet them.

73
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:12,440
I think...

74
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:13,880
there’s no need for that.

75
00:03:14,160 --> 00:03:15,800
But I haven’t met your parents yet.

76
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:17,560
I think it’s really necessary.

77
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:21,160
Is your eye twitching?

78
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:23,120
Uh...

79
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:23,960
You guys enjoy your breakfast.

80
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:26,040
I’ll head to work first.

81
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:29,120
Sis, Qi Miao,

82
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:38,840
why does it feel like she’s upset?

83
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:40,080
Bro,

84
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:41,200
be more confident.

85
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:42,600
Take out the 'feel like.’

86
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:44,400
I already told you,

87
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:46,360
parents are a sensitive topic for my sister.

88
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:48,600
But...

89
00:03:49,320 --> 00:03:51,360
I just wanted to give her a happy birthday.

90
00:03:51,760 --> 00:03:54,840
Celebrating someone’s birthday requires skill.

91
00:03:55,800 --> 00:03:56,200
Come here.

92
00:03:56,600 --> 00:03:57,120
Let me teach you.

93
00:03:59,320 --> 00:04:00,080
Speak properly.

94
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:03,440
Of course, you need to prepare surprises for a birthday.

95
00:04:03,800 --> 00:04:05,200
And the bigger the surprise, the better.

96
00:04:08,480 --> 00:04:09,400
Surprise?

97
00:04:16,520 --> 00:04:18,240
If you meet someone with the same energy as you,

98
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:19,360
and establish a connection,

99
00:04:19,520 --> 00:04:20,920
then you should stay together your whole life,

100
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:22,319
until the end.

101
00:04:26,280 --> 00:04:27,119
What's going on?

102
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:29,160
Why do I keep thinking about him?

103
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:31,520
It must be because this person is too annoying.

104
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:32,800
That has to be it.

105
00:04:33,080 --> 00:04:33,520
No way.

106
00:04:33,800 --> 00:04:34,720
Focus!

107
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:35,920
Work, work, work!

108
00:04:46,440 --> 00:04:47,280
Bye-bye, bye-bye.

109
00:04:47,400 --> 00:04:48,160
See you tomorrow!

110
00:04:59,120 --> 00:04:59,760
Qi Miao.

111
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:09,000
Qi Miao.

112
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:13,520
I bring you a dance performance.

113
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:15,360
Happy

114
00:05:17,520 --> 00:05:18,200
Birthday!

115
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:22,560
Qi Miao!

116
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:23,960
Happy Birthday!

117
00:06:25,800 --> 00:06:27,400
You're so embarrassing me.

118
00:06:28,200 --> 00:06:28,640
Alright.

119
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:29,280
Let's go.

120
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:39,960
It's just a pair of chopsticks.

121
00:06:40,280 --> 00:06:41,400
You can arrange them however you want.

122
00:06:41,880 --> 00:06:44,240
Unless you can make a flower out of them?

123
00:06:45,400 --> 00:06:47,280
Don't you even know what quality of life means?

124
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:50,760
This pair of chopsticks shows your true nature.

125
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:52,920
What's wrong with my nature?

126
00:06:55,280 --> 00:06:57,280
Even if my life isn't simple,

127
00:06:57,960 --> 00:06:59,040
I am,

128
00:06:59,160 --> 00:07:00,040
very down-to-earth.

129
00:07:01,080 --> 00:07:02,480
Not like some people,

130
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:03,920
pretending to be aloof.

131
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:07,880
I’m really happy today.

132
00:07:08,360 --> 00:07:08,880
Thank you.

133
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:09,880
As long as you're happy.

134
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:14,520
Who are you calling pretentious?

135
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:17,000
Say it again if you dare.

136
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:18,920
Every extra second I spend with you,

137
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,360
is pure torture.

138
00:07:20,520 --> 00:07:21,360
So you don’t want to see me?

139
00:07:21,480 --> 00:07:22,600
You can leave, Dad.

140
00:07:22,720 --> 00:07:23,400
Why are you here? Just go!

141
00:07:23,480 --> 00:07:25,080
Why aren't you leaving? You... Dad... Auntie.

142
00:07:25,240 --> 00:07:26,200
Stop arguing, all of you.

143
00:07:26,400 --> 00:07:27,040
I'll take care of this.

144
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:27,760
I'll do it.

145
00:07:30,080 --> 00:07:30,480
Dad.

146
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:31,280
Mom.

147
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:33,320
Why are you here?

148
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:38,120
It's your birthday today.

149
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:39,880
Mom came over to celebrate your birthday.

150
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:41,440
Sweetheart.

151
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:42,760
Happy birthday.

152
00:07:44,320 --> 00:07:45,400
Did you invite them?

153
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:48,160
Sis, happy birthday.

154
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:52,440
Happy birthday to you.

155
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:55,680
Happy birthday to you.

156
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:59,040
Happy birthday to you.

157
00:07:59,160 --> 00:08:00,560
Happy birthday... Alright, alright.

158
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:01,720
Stop singing.

159
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:03,120
After dinner,

160
00:08:03,240 --> 00:08:03,920
everyone goes back home.

161
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:07,880
Miao Miao.

162
00:08:13,320 --> 00:08:13,760
What?

163
00:08:13,880 --> 00:08:14,720
You're not even letting us eat?

164
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:16,160
This is for my daughter.

165
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:18,840
I'm giving it to her myself.

166
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:20,120
Here, eat.

167
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:23,120
I've checked this soup.

168
00:08:23,360 --> 00:08:24,320
It's good for your health.

169
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:26,200
Thank you.

170
00:08:27,680 --> 00:08:28,560
Xiao Hao.

171
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:30,920
Did you cook this whole dinner?

172
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:31,600
Yes, I did.

173
00:08:33,680 --> 00:08:36,720
This young man is not only good-looking but also talented in cooking.

174
00:08:37,400 --> 00:08:38,040
Miao Miao.

175
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:39,440
You really have good taste.

176
00:08:39,599 --> 00:08:40,400
Mom!

177
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:42,120
Miao Miao.

178
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:43,480
Don't listen to your mom rambling.

179
00:08:43,599 --> 00:08:45,680
When finding a boyfriend, looks aren't everything.

180
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:46,680
Character matters too.

181
00:08:46,920 --> 00:08:47,280
Right?

182
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:48,719
What are you even saying?

183
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:50,440
Saying that,

184
00:08:50,560 --> 00:08:52,320
how do you think Xiao Hao would feel?

185
00:08:53,120 --> 00:08:53,880
It's okay.

186
00:08:55,720 --> 00:08:56,400
Miaomiao,

187
00:08:56,920 --> 00:08:57,640
early this morning,

188
00:08:57,760 --> 00:08:58,600
Xiao Hao called us,

189
00:08:58,720 --> 00:09:00,280
inviting us to celebrate your birthday.

190
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:03,160
It's very thoughtful of him,

191
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:04,520
really rare to see these days.

192
00:09:09,080 --> 00:09:10,560
I think this young man is quite remarkable.

193
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:11,520
Miaomiao,

194
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:14,440
Dad is very pleased.

195
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:16,200
Dad,

196
00:09:16,280 --> 00:09:17,680
we're just roommates.

197
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:18,560
Roommates?

198
00:09:19,040 --> 00:09:19,440
Come on,

199
00:09:20,520 --> 00:09:21,000
come on,

200
00:09:24,760 --> 00:09:25,960
where are you from?

201
00:09:26,840 --> 00:09:28,400
What do you do for a living?

202
00:09:29,480 --> 00:09:30,120
Oh, sorry.

203
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:31,800
I haven't introduced myself yet.

204
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:33,120
I'm from Bluecore Star,

205
00:09:33,240 --> 00:09:34,440
a Star Envoy of Bluecore Star.

206
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:36,960
Bluecore Star?

207
00:09:37,800 --> 00:09:38,680
Never heard of it.

208
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:41,080
Is it some remote little town?

209
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:41,720
Far away?

210
00:09:41,880 --> 00:09:42,400
Far.

211
00:09:42,520 --> 00:09:43,760
Farther than you could ever imagine.

212
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:46,320
Miaomiao,

213
00:09:46,480 --> 00:09:50,000
how far have you two progressed?

214
00:09:50,560 --> 00:09:51,040
Auntie,

215
00:09:51,560 --> 00:09:54,680
with my years of battlefield experience in love,

216
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:56,480
I can tell they've definitely already...

217
00:09:56,600 --> 00:09:57,400
Qi Dongdong!

218
00:09:57,600 --> 00:09:58,840
Why are you everywhere?

219
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:00,480
Even food can't shut you up, can it?

220
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:03,240
We've already established a connection.
